Focuses on monitoring LLM requests and tracking their performance.
Extends the Week 2 provider-agnostic LLM client.
Tracks input tokens and output tokens for every request.
Measures response time (latency) and estimates API cost.
Uses MongoDB to store successful and failed request details.
Implements timeouts and retry mechanisms to handle temporary failures.

Output: LLM usage records containing token counts, response time, estimated cost and request status are stored in MongoDB.
